nsight-gpu-trace
================

This is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or
endorsed by NVIDIA Corporation.

The crate contains hand-written runtime compatibility declarations for the
NVIDIA PerfWorks host API exposed by libnvperf_grfx_host.so on Linux and
nvperf_grfx_host.dll on Windows. Their function names, parameter layouts,
metric conventions, and behavior were derived from the public NVIDIA Nsight
Perf SDK documentation and nvperf_host.h. NVIDIA SDK headers and binaries carry
their own license terms and are not redistributed by this package. Users are
responsible for obtaining a compatible Nsight Graphics/PerfWorks installation
and complying with its license.

The protobuf schema is not copied into this project. At runtime the crate
recovers descriptors embedded in the user's installed WarpViz plugin binary.
Metric formulas and counter data are likewise supplied only by the user's
installed NVIDIA library and capture.

Documentation consulted during design:

- https://docs.nvidia.com/nsight-graphics/UserGuide/gpu-trace-overview.html
- https://docs.nvidia.com/nsight-graphics/UserGuide/gpu-trace-ui.html
- https://docs.nvidia.com/nsight-graphics/UserGuide/gpu-trace-system-architecture.html
- https://docs.nvidia.com/nsight-graphics/UserGuide/shader-profiler.html
- https://developer.nvidia.com/nsight-perf-sdk

The CLI workflow also took inspiration from Luna5ama/Alpha-Piscium's
nsight-graphics-analyzer skill. This crate decodes WRPV captures directly and
does not include that project's code or exported data.

NVIDIA, Nsight, PerfWorks, Vulkan, and OpenGL names belong to their respective
owners.
